provider-events-hint = With a secret set, the identity provider can report changes (a user disabled, a role or group changed) to POST /api/v1/identity-provider/events with the header "Authorization: Bearer" and the secret. The sync then runs within seconds instead of at its next interval. The report only starts a run: the sync reads the provider itself.
provider-events-needs-sync = Events only start the sync, which is not running on this instance.
provider-events-off = Off: changes are picked up at the sync's next interval.
provider-events-none-yet = On. No event has arrived yet.
provider-events-last = On. Last event { $when }.
provider-events-secret-once = Copy it now: it is shown only once. Enter it in the identity provider's event listener. A new secret replaces this one at once.
provider-events-create = Create secret
provider-events-rotate = New secret
provider-events-delete = Turn off
provider-events-delete-question = Turn events off? The provider's reports are refused; the sync still runs at its interval.
provider-events-delete-yes = Turn off
oidc-sync-not-configured = Not set up. Without it, someone disabled at the identity provider keeps access until their sign-in ends. Set oidc.sync.client_secret: it is required for production.
oidc-sync-switched-off = Switched off by oidc.sync.is_enabled = false. Someone disabled at the identity provider keeps access until their sign-in ends. It is required for production.
oidc-sync-dry-run = Dry run: the sync only reports what it would change and changes nothing.
oidc-sync-stale = { $count ->
    [one] The sync has not run for more than one interval. Check the identity provider and the service account.
   *[other] The sync has not run for more than { $count } intervals. Check the identity provider and the service account.
}
oidc-sync-held = { $count ->
    [one] The safety brake is holding back 1 deactivation.
   *[other] The safety brake is holding back { $count } deactivations.
}
oidc-sync-held-hint = This looks more like a mistake at the identity provider than like people leaving. Check the provider first: if it was a mistake, fix it there and this list clears by itself. Other leavers are still deactivated as usual.
oidc-sync-leavers-held = { $count ->
    [one] This app reached its daily limit of automatic removals: { $count } more person who left waits to be removed from all chats by an admin.
   *[other] This app reached its daily limit of automatic removals: { $count } more people who left wait to be removed from all chats by an admin.
  }
oidc-sync-confirm = Confirm these deactivations
oidc-sync-confirm-question = { $count ->
    [one] Deactivate this person now? Their sessions end at once. This is undone when the identity provider enables them again.
   *[other] Deactivate these { $count } people now? Their sessions end at once. This is undone when the identity provider enables them again.
}
oidc-sync-confirm-yes = Yes, deactivate
oidc-sync-confirmed = Confirmed
oidc-sync-cause-removed = removed from the identity provider
oidc-sync-cause-disabled = disabled at the identity provider
oidc-sync-cause-no-role = no TeamCraft role left at the identity provider
oidc-sync-cause-other = other reason
oidc-sync-never-ran = Has not run yet.
oidc-sync-last-run = Last run
oidc-sync-outcome = Result
oidc-sync-changes-title = Changes
oidc-sync-duration = { $when }, took { $seconds } s
oidc-sync-outcome-ok = Finished
oidc-sync-outcome-partial = Finished with errors: some changes failed and are tried again next run
oidc-sync-outcome-held = Finished, safety brake engaged
oidc-sync-outcome-dry-run = Finished as a dry run
oidc-sync-outcome-failed = Failed, nothing was changed
oidc-sync-error-unreachable = The identity provider did not answer.
oidc-sync-error-refused = The identity provider refused the service account.
oidc-sync-error-invalid = The identity provider sent an unexpected answer.
oidc-sync-error-no-users = The identity provider listed no users.
oidc-sync-error-database = The database refused.
oidc-sync-failures = { $count } failures in a row.
oidc-sync-changes = { $deactivated } deactivated, { $reactivated } reactivated, { $roles } role changes, { $groups } group changes, { $failed } failed
oidc-sync-unfinished = { $count ->
    [one] 1 deactivation is still being finished; access is already refused.
   *[other] { $count } deactivations are still being finished; access is already refused.
}
oidc-sync-pending-removals = { $count ->
    [one] 1 deactivated account still has devices in encryption groups. Only an admin's "Remove from all chats" takes them out.
   *[other] { $count } deactivated accounts still have devices in encryption groups. Only an admin's "Remove from all chats" takes them out.
}
oidc-sync-open-users = Open Users
oidc-sync-preview = Check what a run would change
oidc-sync-preview-title = What a run would change now
oidc-sync-preview-summary = { $deactivate } deactivated, { $held } held back, { $reactivate } reactivated, { $roles } role changes. A run may deactivate { $allowed } of { $active } active users.
health-detail-held = { $count ->
    [one] 1 deactivation is waiting for a decision.
   *[other] { $count } deactivations are waiting for a decision.
}
health-check-oidc_sync_brake = Identity provider sync: safety brake
health-check-oidc_sync_brake-hint = Holds deactivations back when a run would deactivate too many people at once. Fails while any are waiting for a decision.
health-check-retention = Retention job
health-check-retention-hint = Deletes what is past its retention. Late after three missed runs.
health-check-partition_maintenance = Message partitions
health-check-partition_maintenance-hint = Creates the storage for coming months ahead of time. Late after three missed runs.
health-check-backup = Backup
health-check-backup-hint = Reported by the deployment. Fails when the last backup is older than the limit in Settings.
health-check-certificate = Certificate
health-check-certificate-hint = Reported by the deployment. Fails when the served certificate expires within the limit in Settings.
health-check-disk_space = Disk space
health-check-disk_space-hint = Reported by the deployment. Fails when the disk is fuller than the limit in Settings.
health-check-holiday_feed = Holiday feed
health-check-holiday_feed-hint = The iCalendar feed of public holidays set under Settings. Fails when its copy is older than the limit there, or when no fetch has worked yet. Off without a feed.
health-check-holiday_resync = Holidays in calendars
health-check-holiday_resync-hint = Writes the calendar events of repeating meetings that skip public holidays again when the holidays change, and once a week. Fails when it hasn't got through for three weeks, usually because the calendar server refuses or is down. Off without meetings.
policy-owners-hint = Owners keep the workspace in order, and their apps sign the admin roster and this policy by themselves. Keep at least two: if the only owner leaves or loses all devices and the recovery kit, nobody can manage the workspace again. To replace an owner, add the new one first.
roster-by-hand = Change the roster by hand
roster-signing-no-role-claim = Roles can't follow the identity provider by themselves yet, because its ID tokens don't carry them. Your operator needs to add the role mapper; see "Role signing" in the operations guide. Until then, change roles below by hand.
roster-signing-no-key-claim = Roles can't follow the identity provider by themselves yet, because it doesn't keep the attribute with people's identity keys. Your operator needs to set it up; see "Role signing" in the operations guide. Until then, change roles below by hand.
roster-signing-provider-changed-detail = This app's sign-in comes from { $issuer }, not from the identity provider the workspace trusts, so roles aren't changed by themselves. If you moved to a new provider on purpose, choose "Trust the provider I sign in with next" below.
policy-role-signing = Who signs role changes
policy-role-signing-automatic = Owners' apps, following the identity provider (recommended)
policy-role-signing-manual = An owner, by hand
policy-role-signing-hint = Automatic means whoever controls the identity provider can appoint admins, as far as they can already sign in as people. Admins can't read old content either way. By hand, an owner has to confirm every change here.
policy-key-attestation = Colleagues' keys
policy-key-attestation-optional = Confirmed by the identity provider where possible (recommended)
policy-key-attestation-required = Only keys the identity provider confirmed
policy-key-attestation-hint = Apps check with the identity provider that a colleague's key is theirs, so a compromised server can't slip in a fake one. For now this covers owners and admins, whose provider accounts the owners' apps signed; other members' keys are trusted on first use either way. "Only confirmed keys" refuses unconfirmed keys of owners and admins. Keys apps trusted before stay trusted.
policy-role-owner-name = Owner role at the identity provider
policy-role-admin-name = Admin role at the identity provider
policy-role-names-hint = The client roles that make somebody an owner or admin. Only change them if your identity provider uses other names.
policy-role-name-empty = Enter the name of the role. Saved empty, it goes back to the usual name.
policy-role-provider = Trusted identity provider: { $issuer }
policy-role-provider-reset = Trust the provider I sign in with next
policy-role-provider-details = Identity provider settings
roster-signing-reported-gone = The server reports that { $names } no longer holds an admin role. Unless the identity provider says otherwise, they come off the roster in a few days, one at a time. If that's wrong, check the server: nothing else is needed.
roster-signing-awaiting-owner = The identity provider makes you an owner. That's in force as soon as another owner's app has been open. If no other owner is left, ask your operator to give the former owner their role back for a moment.

policy-scheduled = Scheduled messages
policy-scheduled-hint = The server holds these encrypted and releases them at their time, whether their author's devices are on or not. It enforces this rule.
policy-scheduled-enabled = People can schedule messages
policy-scheduled-enabled-hint = Off: "Send later" goes away, and messages already scheduled don't go out by themselves: they wait until their owner sends or cancels them.
policy-scheduled-horizon = How far ahead
policy-scheduled-cap = Waiting messages per person
admin-channel-restore = Restore
admin-channel-archive-confirm = Archive this channel for everyone? Its members can still read it but nobody can post, and it leaves their lists. Nothing is deleted, and you can restore it here.
admin-guests-filter = Show
admin-guests-filter-all = All guests
admin-guests-filter-expiring = Expiring soon
admin-guests-filter-no-sponsor = Without a sponsor
admin-guests-filter-never = Never signed in
admin-guests-sponsor-placeholder = Search by sponsor name…
admin-guests-any = Any
admin-guests-bulk = Selected guests
admin-guests-selected = { $count ->
    [one] { $count } guest selected
   *[other] { $count } guests selected
}
admin-guests-select = Select { $name }
admin-guests-remove = Remove
admin-guests-remove-confirm = { $count ->
    [one] Remove this guest now? They lose access to the space and its channels, and their sponsor is not told. Their messages stay under the retention rules.
   *[other] Remove these { $count } guests now? They lose access to the space and its channels, and their sponsors are not told. Their messages stay under the retention rules.
}
admin-guests-never = Never signed in
admin-guests-no-sponsor = No sponsor
admin-guests-no-expiry = Never
policy-guest-notices = Notices before a guest's access ends
policy-guest-notices-hint = The guest, their sponsor and the space's admins get a notice in the app. The guest and the sponsor also get a mail, which names no guest and no space.
policy-guest-notices-default = 14 and 3 days before
policy-guest-notices-long = 30, 14 and 3 days before
policy-guest-notices-short = 7 and 1 day before
policy-guest-notices-off = No notices
policy-guest-sponsor-extension = How far sponsors may extend a guest
policy-guest-sponsor-extension-hint = From today. Admins aren't limited.
policy-guest-sponsor-none = Sponsors may not extend
policy-guest-sponsor-days = { $count ->
    [one] Up to { $count } day
   *[other] Up to { $count } days
}
audit-guest-extended = Guest extended
audit-channel-restored = Channel restored
admin-guests-skipped = { $count ->
    [one] One of them never expires and is left out when extending.
   *[other] { $count } of them never expire and are left out when extending.
}

## Problem reports (docs/bug-reports.md)
policy-bug-reports = Problem reports
policy-bug-reports-hint = "Report a problem" sends a person's description, an optional screenshot and the app's recent log, end-to-end encrypted, as a direct message. Choose who receives them.
policy-bug-reports-admins = Owners and admins
policy-bug-reports-admins-hint = Everyone with a role in the workspace's signed admin list. Nothing to set up.
policy-bug-reports-named = These people
policy-bug-reports-named-hint = For example the people who look after TeamCraft. Until you pick someone, reports go to the owners and admins.
policy-bug-reports-chosen = Recipients of problem reports

## Inactive channels and idle guest accounts (issue #212)
policy-guest-deactivate = Deactivate a local guest account after its last space ended
policy-guest-deactivate-never = Never
policy-guest-deactivate-hint = Applies to guests with a password of their own that belong to no space any more. The account is only deactivated, not deleted, and an admin can reactivate it.
policy-inactivity = Inactive channels
policy-inactivity-hint = The server only sees when the last message was stored, never what it says. Off by default: nothing is noticed, archived or deleted until you turn it on.
policy-inactivity-enable = Look after channels nobody writes in
policy-inactivity-enable-hint = The owners of a quiet channel get a mail first. The channel is archived later only if nobody writes in it or keeps it open. Channels nobody can be told about are left alone.
policy-inactivity-notice = Tell the owners after this long without a message
policy-inactivity-archive = Archive after the notice
policy-inactivity-archive-hint = Archived channels stay readable and an admin can restore them. With "notices only" nothing is archived.
policy-inactivity-notice-only = Notices only, never archive
policy-inactivity-snooze = Keeping a channel open lasts
policy-inactivity-limit = Most channels per run
policy-inactivity-limit-hint = A safety limit for noticing, archiving and deleting each, per hourly run. The audit log says when it held something back.
policy-inactivity-channels = { $count ->
    [one] { $count } channel
   *[other] { $count } channels
  }
policy-inactivity-delete = Delete channels the policy archived
policy-inactivity-delete-never = Never
policy-inactivity-delete-hint = The only way this policy deletes messages. It deletes only channels it archived itself and nobody restored, and the owners are warned 7 days before. Cannot be undone.
admin-inactivity-notified = The owners were told that this channel is quiet.
admin-inactivity-archive-on = Archived on { $date } unless somebody writes in it or keeps it open.
admin-inactivity-archived = Archived automatically because it was quiet.
admin-inactivity-delete-on = Deleted on { $date } unless somebody restores it or postpones the deletion.
admin-inactivity-kept-open = Kept open until { $date }.
admin-inactivity-keep-open = Keep open
admin-inactivity-postpone-delete = Postpone deletion
audit-inactivity-notice = Owners told about a quiet channel
audit-channel-auto-archived = Quiet channel archived
audit-channel-auto-deleted = Archived channel deleted
audit-inactivity-snoozed = Channel kept open
audit-inactivity-limited = Inactivity run stopped at its limit
audit-space-archived = Space archived with its channels
audit-space-restored = Space restored
